Hi Raj,

I have reviewed the requirements. Here is my engineering assessment:

1. Torque: 450 Nm at output — our HG-450 model handles this with 10% margin.
2. Speed ratio: 1450/120 = 12.08:1 — we will use a 12:1 ratio gearbox.
3. Shaft: 42mm output, 28mm input — standard sizes, no issue.
4. Tolerance ±0.05mm on output shaft — achievable with our CNC grinding process.
5. Mounting: Flange B5 with M16 bolts — confirmed.

Material recommendation:
- Housing: Cast iron (FG260 grade)
- Gears: EN8 with case hardening to 58 HRC
- Output shaft: EN19 (better fatigue strength than EN8 for this application)

TBD - efficiency class IE2 or IE3. Please confirm which one you need for the motor.

Regarding the IP55 protection, we will use double lip seals and a breather valve.

Weight of complete assembly: 92 kg (with oil fill).
Noise level: less than 75 dB at rated speed.

I will prepare the GA drawing with dimensions 580mm × 420mm × 380mm (L×W×H). Expected to share by next week.

Please confirm the paint shade — RAL 7035 (light grey) is our standard. Let me know if you need a different shade.

